First, perform the requested integration.

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\displaystyle\int\limits_{0}^{1}{f\left( x \right)dx}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\int_0^1\sum_{n=0}^{\infty }(-1)^n\dfrac{n+1}{ 5^n}x^ndx
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\sum_{n=0}^{\infty }\int_0^1(-1)^n\dfrac{n+1}{ 5^n}x^ndx
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\left. \sum_{n=0}^{\infty }(-1)^n\dfrac{n+1}{ 5^n}\dfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1} \right|_{0}^{1}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\sum_{n=0}^{\infty }{\dfrac{(-1)^n}{{{5}^n}}}
\end{align}$
